<title>ITALY: Bank of Italy buying back up to 2.75 trln lire BOT.</title>
<headline>Bank of Italy buying back up to 2.75 trln lire BOT.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Italy said it would buy back up to 2.75 trillion lire of short-term bills (BOT) expiring between January 31 and April 28, 1997.</p>
<p>Bids must be received by 0930 GMT.</p>
</text>
